      "source": [
        "## Step 3: Data analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "Se muestran estadísticas descriptivas del dataset."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "47c2e2f8",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "47c2e2f8"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Describe data\n",
        "df_sal.describe()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "15a49ad7",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "15a49ad7"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Step 3: Data distribution\n",
        "\n",
        "Se representa la distribución de la columna `Salary` con Seaborn."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "495acb7c",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "495acb7c"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Data distribution\n",
        "plt.title('Salary Distribution Plot')\n",
        "sns.distplot(df_sal['Salary'])\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "2ea7efd0",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "2ea7efd0"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Relationship between Salary and Experience\n",
        "\n",
        "Se crea una gráfica de dispersión de experiencia contra salario."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "9cc3e9ec",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "9cc3e9ec"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Relationship between Salary and Experience\n",
        "plt.scatter(df_sal['YearsExperience'], df_sal['Salary'], color = 'lightcoral')\n",
        "plt.title('Salary vs Experience')\n",
        "plt.xlabel('Years of Experience')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('Salary')\n",
        "plt.box(False)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "62b2343b",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "62b2343b"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Step 4: Split the dataset into dependent/independent variables\n",
        "\n",
        "`X` contiene la variable independiente y `y` la variable dependiente."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "4e16fc6f",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4e16fc6f"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Splitting variables\n",
        "X = df_sal.iloc[:, :1]  # independent\n",
        "y = df_sal.iloc[:, 1:]  # dependent"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "d93af55d",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "d93af55d"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Step 4: Split data into Train/Test sets\n",
        "\n",
        "Se utiliza 80 % para entrenamiento y 20 % para prueba."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "5ee3b281",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5ee3b281"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Splitting dataset into test/train\n",
        "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(X, y, test_size = 0.2, random_state = 0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "dc7ee977",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "dc7ee977"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Step 5: Train the regression model\n",
        "\n",
        "Se crea `LinearRegression` y se entrena con los datos de entrenamiento."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "a44c16cd",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "a44c16cd"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Regressor model\n",
        "regressor = LinearRegression()\n",
        "regressor.fit(X_train, y_train)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "a994f73c",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "a994f73c"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Step 6: Predict the result\n",
        "\n",
        "Se generan predicciones para los conjuntos de prueba y entrenamiento."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "8d769389",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8d769389"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Prediction result\n",
        "y_pred_test = regressor.predict(X_test)     # predicted value of y_test\n",
        "y_pred_train = regressor.predict(X_train)   # predicted value of y_train"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "63eb8c44",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "63eb8c44"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Step 7: Plot training set data vs predictions\n",
        "\n",
        "Se dibujan los datos de entrenamiento y la línea predicha por el modelo."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "0a63190a",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0a63190a"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Prediction on training set\n",
        "plt.scatter(X_train, y_train, color = 'lightcoral')\n",
        "plt.plot(X_train, y_pred_train, color = 'firebrick')\n",
        "plt.title('Salary vs Experience (Training Set)')\n",
        "plt.xlabel('Years of Experience')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('Salary')\n",
        "plt.legend(['X_train/Pred(y_test)', 'X_train/y_train'], title = 'Sal/Exp', loc='best', facecolor='white')\n",
        "plt.box(False)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "0997d2ac",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0997d2ac"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Step 7: Plot test set data vs predictions\n",
        "\n",
        "Se dibujan los datos de prueba junto con la línea de regresión mostrada por el artículo."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "8532e48e",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8532e48e"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Prediction on test set\n",
        "plt.scatter(X_test, y_test, color = 'lightcoral')\n",
        "plt.plot(X_train, y_pred_train, color = 'firebrick')\n",
        "plt.title('Salary vs Experience (Test Set)')\n",
        "plt.xlabel('Years of Experience')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('Salary')\n",
        "plt.legend(['X_train/Pred(y_test)', 'X_train/y_train'], title = 'Sal/Exp', loc='best', facecolor='white')\n",
        "plt.box(False)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
